id: 6
hanzi: 辩论
pinyin: biàn lùn
level: HSK 5
part_of_speech: Verb / Noun

meanings_summary:
  en: to debate; to argue logically; debate; formal argumentation
  es: debatir; polemizar; debate; argumentación reglada

senses[2]{sense_number,part_of_speech,register,definition_en,definition_es,example_phrase}:
  1 | Verb | Standard | to present logical arguments, refute opponent propositions, and debate formally on a specific topic | exponer argumentos lógicos, rebatir tesis contrarias y debatir formalmente sobre un tema | 就此问题展开激烈辩论 (debate fiercely on this question)
  2 | Noun | Standard | a formal structured competition, parliamentary contest, or academic debate | competición formal de oratoria, certamen parlamentario o debate académico reglado | 国际大专辩论赛 (international collegiate debate competition)

example_sentences[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 两支代表队在全国大学生辩论赛决赛中妙语连珠，就科技发展与环境保护的关系展开了精彩辩论。 | Liǎng zhī dàibiǎotuán zài quánguó dàxuéshēng biànlùnsài juésài zhōng miàoyǔ-liánzhū, jiù kējì fāzhǎn yǔ huánjìng bǎohù de guānxi zhǎnkāi le jīngcǎi biànlùn. | In the national collegiate debate finals, both teams exchanged witty arguments, holding a splendid debate on technology and ecology. | En la final del torneo nacional de debate, ambos equipos cruzaron brillantes argumentos sobre tecnología y medio ambiente.
  #2 | 为了验证辩论中的学术假说，斯坦福重金聘请专业摄影师在操场跑道旁架设相机，开创了实验科学的新范式。 | Wèile yànzhèng biànlùn zhōng de xuéshù jiǎshuō, Sītǎnfú zhòngjīn pìnqǐng zhuānyè shèyǐngshī zài cāochǎng pǎodào páng jiàshè xiàngjī, kāichuàng le shíyàn kēxué de xīn fànshì. | To verify the hypothesis raised in debate, Stanford hired a photographer to set up cameras beside the track, pioneering experimental science. | Para verificar la hipótesis de su debate, Stanford contrató a un fotógrafo que montó cámaras junto a la pista, inaugurando un hito científico.

collocations[6]{hanzi,en}:
  辩论赛 | debate competition
  激烈辩论 | heated debate
